 "2_inequality": "Exact shear equation in these variables: d(alpha'-beta')/dt = -Theta (alpha'-beta') + (3/2) S, S = -(4/3) eta (alpha'-beta') quasi-statically => sigma'/sigma = |Theta| - 2 kappa eta. With Theta'/Theta = (1+w)|Theta|/2 in a power-law contraction, d ln Sigma^2/dt = (1-w)|Theta| - 4 kappa eta. Causality eta = c^2 tau (rho+p), Knudsen tau|Theta| = K, Theta^2 = 3 kappa rho: net damping of Sigma^2 iff c^2 K > 3(1-w)/(4(1+w)). (A first estimate used kappa eta >= |Theta| and a threshold (1+w)c^2K >= 3; the numerical test contradicted it and the derivation was corrected.)"
}